cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you reference this analysis, please cite it as below.
title: "One PR, a million lines of Rust: what Bun's AI-assisted rewrite did to its bug reports"
authors:
  - family-names: Smyshliaev
    given-names: Aleksandr
date-released: 2026-08-10
url: "https://github.com/asmyshlyaev177/bun-rust-rewrite-analysis"
abstract: >-
  An observational study of oven-sh/bun issue-tracker data across the May 2026
  Zig-to-Rust rewrite (PR #30412): 2,981 issues over 39 merge-anchored weeks,
  with bug reports classified by the build they name. Canary-channel bug
  reports rose 2.2-3.5x while the fix rate held (43.5% to 41.9%); stable-only
  reports fell 31%; no stable release shipped in the 89 days after the merge.
keywords:
  - rust
  - zig
  - bun
  - ai-assisted-development
  - empirical-software-engineering
